# Port the NestJS API listens on
PORT=4000

# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins (the Next.js frontend URL) —
# also used for the WebSocket gateway's CORS policy.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,https://ai-bot-new-seven.vercel.app

# PostgreSQL connection string for the TradeSignal table (Prisma)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/ai-bot?schema=public"

# Max signals the bot may generate per calendar day — SAFETY CAP, hard-capped
# at 10 regardless of what's set here. A ceiling the market-movement-first
# engine may never reach on a quiet day (0-3 trades is expected and fine) —
# never a quota it tries to fill. See the module doc in signals.service.ts.
MAX_DAILY_SIGNALS=10

# Daily loss circuit breaker — once this many signals resolve STOPLOSS_HIT
# (the original, un-trailed risk stop) on the same IST date, signal
# generation halts entirely for the rest of the day. TRAIL_STOP_HIT and
# TIME_EXIT don't count — neither is ever a full-risk loss. SAFETY CAP,
# hard-capped at 4 regardless of what's set here.
MAX_DAILY_STOPLOSS_HITS=4

# DAILY LOSS CIRCUIT BREAKER (total) — added 2026-09-17, tighter/broader
# than MAX_DAILY_STOPLOSS_HITS above: trips once this many of TODAY's
# resolved trades closed with a negative netCashINR, at ANY terminal status
# (not just STOPLOSS_HIT — a TIME_EXIT can also close negative). SAFETY
# CAP, hard-capped at 10.
MAX_DAILY_LOSSES=3

# DAILY LOSS CIRCUIT BREAKER (consecutive) — added 2026-09-17: trips once
# this many of today's MOST RECENT resolutions, in an unbroken streak, are
# STOPLOSS_HIT — a TARGET_HIT/TRAIL_STOP_HIT in between resets the streak.
# SAFETY CAP, hard-capped at 5.
MAX_CONSECUTIVE_LOSSES=2

# TESTING MODE — set to "false" to bypass the daily signal cap and ALL
# loss circuit breakers above (evaluation never halts for any of them).
# Overrides the ENABLE_DAILY_LIMIT constant at the top of signals.service.ts
# when set. Leave unset/"true" for live trading.
ENABLE_DAILY_LIMIT=true

# SESSION WINDOW UPPER LIMITS — a supplementary cap, independent of the daily
# cap above, on how many NEW positions may be opened within each named
# intraday window (caps, not goals — a quiet window takes 0 trades):
#   Morning   09:15–10:30 IST → max SESSION_CAP_MORNING
#   Mid-Day   10:30–13:15 IST → max SESSION_CAP_MIDDAY
#   Afternoon 13:15–14:30 IST → max SESSION_CAP_AFTERNOON
# The stricter PIVOT/FALLBACK-only structural confirmation (daily pivots,
# session VWAP, or the morning high/low — not a locally-detected intraday
# swing) now applies to EVERY window, not just Mid-Day (tightened
# 2026-09-16) — see SignalsService.passesStructuralReactionFilter().
# NO NEW TRADES AFTER 14:30 IST (per desk request, 2026-09-17) — cut off
# earlier than the old 15:15 boundary. Existing open positions are
# unaffected; they're still tracked/exited as usual, including the
# mandatory EOD square-off at 15:15 (EOD_SQUAREOFF_MINUTES_BEFORE_CLOSE
# below). Change AFTERNOON's endMinutes in market-hours.util.ts to move
# this cutoff — it isn't a plain .env value.
SESSION_CAP_MORNING=4
SESSION_CAP_MIDDAY=2
SESSION_CAP_AFTERNOON=4

# GLOBAL LOSS COOLDOWN GUARD — refactored 2026-09-17. Was: same-direction
# only, triggered by ANY resolution (win or loss). Now: once ANY trade
# resolves at a LOSS (negative netCashINR, any status), BOTH directions are
# rejected for this many minutes — to stop overtrading through a bad patch
# instead of just overtrading one side of it. A win no longer triggers any
# cooldown. Independent of ENABLE_DAILY_LIMIT — stays active even in
# testing mode.
REENTRY_COOLDOWN_MINUTES=15

# SAME-STRIKE LOSS BLACKLIST — after a trade resolves STOPLOSS_HIT, that
# exact (strikePrice, direction) — e.g. 23,400 PE — is rejected for this many
# minutes, so the bot doesn't immediately re-enter the strike that just
# stopped it out in a choppy zone. Only STOPLOSS_HIT blacklists a strike;
# TARGET_HIT/TRAIL_STOP_HIT/TIME_EXIT don't. Set well above a session's
# length (e.g. 999) to blacklist for the rest of the day instead.
STRIKE_BLACKLIST_MINUTES=45

# Yahoo Finance symbol for the Nifty 50 index
NIFTY_SYMBOL=^NSEI

# Strike step used to round to the nearest ATM strike
STRIKE_STEP=50

# --- Risk protocol (fixed to 1 lot, ATM delta proxy 0.5) --------------------
# Contract units per lot
LOT_SIZE=65
# Proxy delta used to translate index-point moves into option-premium moves
DELTA_PROXY=0.5

# --- Exit sizing: volatility-based (ATR), not fixed points ------------------
# Stop-loss/target distances scale with the market's own recent volatility:
#   indexTargetPoints   = ATR(14) x ATR_TARGET_MULTIPLIER
#   indexStopLossPoints = ATR(14) x ATR_STOPLOSS_MULTIPLIER
# A wider/choppier session naturally gets more room; a quiet one gets pulled
# in tighter. The 2:1 default is the standard volatility-sized reward:risk
# convention. Cash P&L figures are then fully derived from these distances
# (no separate fixed rupee constant to keep in sync).
ATR_TARGET_MULTIPLIER=2
ATR_STOPLOSS_MULTIPLIER=1
# FIXED TARGET (added 2026-09-21) — when > 0, every trade's target is this
# many rupees of profit per lot (1 lot, DELTA_PROXY, LOT_SIZE), regardless of
# ATR or nearby pivots: target points = TARGET_CASH_INR / (DELTA_PROXY x
# LOT_SIZE), so 1100 -> ~33.85 Nifty points (~16.9 option points). The stop
# stays volatility-based (ATR_STOPLOSS_MULTIPLIER x ATR). ATR_TARGET_MULTIPLIER
# and pivot target-snapping are then unused. Set to 0 to go back to the
# ATR/pivot-based target. NOTE: a setup whose stop would cost more than this
# target (ATR above ~34pts) is rejected by the min-profit filter below.
TARGET_CASH_INR=1100

# --- Dynamic min-profit filter -------------------------------------------------
# Minimum target payoff (1 lot, INR) a setup must clear to be taken at all —
# the greater of MIN_TARGET_CASH_FLOOR_INR (a minimum-anticipated-move floor,
# in option premium terms) and ATR(14) x DELTA_PROXY x LOT_SIZE x
# MIN_TARGET_ATR_FRACTION (scales with the market's own current volatility,
# so a quiet-ATR day isn't blocked by one fixed rupee figure the way a static
# floor alone would). Replaces the old fixed MIN_TARGET_CASH_INR. See the
# filter in SignalsService.refreshSignal().
# 650 = 10 CE/PE option points x the 65 LOT_SIZE below — the minimum
# anticipated option-premium move a setup must offer to be worth taking.
MIN_TARGET_CASH_FLOOR_INR=650
MIN_TARGET_ATR_FRACTION=0.5

# --- RSI directional bands -----------------------------------------------------
# SignalsService.evaluateStrategy() uses one continuous RSI band per
# direction (not two disjoint bands with a dead gap between them):
#   BULLISH: spot > SMA9 AND (50+RSI_NEUTRAL_HALFWIDTH) <= RSI14 <= RSI_MAX
#   BEARISH: spot < SMA9 AND RSI_MIN <= RSI14 <= (50-RSI_NEUTRAL_HALFWIDTH)
# Outside those: the tight neutral zone around 50 (no directional edge), or
# beyond RSI_MIN/RSI_MAX (extreme exhaustion, too likely to mean-revert).
RSI_NEUTRAL_HALFWIDTH=2
RSI_MAX=85
RSI_MIN=15

# --- Market-Movement-First Signal Engine: ATR expansion (softened) -----------
# The SMA(9)/RSI(14) read alone can't tell a genuine breakout from a flat
# chop that happens to sit in the right zone. IndicatorsService.computeSnapshot()
# computes atrExpansionRatio = ATR14-now / ATR14-N-bars-ago (N =
# ATR_EXPANSION_LOOKBACK_BARS, fixed in code — a structural constant of the
# indicator pipeline, not a per-desk knob). SignalsService.refreshSignal()
# then passes the expansion check when EITHER holds:
#   1. atrExpansionRatio >= ATR_EXPANSION_MIN_RATIO (default 1.05 — requires
#      ATR to still be genuinely expanding, not just elevated-but-cooling;
#      raised from 0.9 on 2026-09-16 after fading-momentum setups under the
#      looser threshold were only carrying a few points before reversing), OR
#   2. ATR14 is already >= ATR_BASELINE_POINTS in absolute index points
#      (real movement is self-evident regardless of the recent ATR trend).
# ATR_BASELINE_POINTS was raised to 18 on 2026-09-18 and put back to 12 on
# 2026-09-21: at 18 it blocked steady-trend days (ATR flat at ~12-16, ratio
# ~1.0), and a 40-day replay showed the entries it blocked did no worse than
# the ones it let through.
ATR_EXPANSION_MIN_RATIO=1.05
ATR_BASELINE_POINTS=12

# --- Market regime / chop filter (added 2026-09-17, tightened 2026-09-18) -------
# ATR expansion above only measures whether volatility is present, not
# whether it's DIRECTIONAL — a choppy back-and-forth session can carry a
# respectable ATR while still being a bad environment for a directional
# entry. IndicatorsService.computeADX() / computeChoppinessIndex() feed
# SignalsService's check, which requires BOTH:
#   1. ADX(14) >= ADX_THRESHOLD (classic Wilder trend-strength reading,
#      direction-agnostic)
#   2. Choppiness Index(14) <= CHOPPINESS_INDEX_MAX (0-100 scale; low means
#      price covered real net ground over the period, not just oscillation)
# Changed from OR to AND (2026-09-18) — OR let a real trade through on
# adx14=12.4 (failed) alone passing via chop14=58.8, barely under the 60
# ceiling; that trade peaked only 1.5pts favorable before reversing. Each
# side still fails OPEN (passes) on its own when there isn't yet enough
# candle history for the calculation to stabilize — same cold-start
# convention as the ATR expansion check above — but a real failing reading
# on either side now blocks regardless of the other.
# NOTE: a literal "current 5m volume >= 1.5x its 20-period SMA" gate was
# considered and deliberately NOT implemented — Yahoo Finance reports
# volume=0 for the ^NSEI index feed this bot trades (confirmed live;
# indices carry no traded volume of their own, only their constituent
# stocks do), so that comparison would be a permanent 0-vs-0 no-op rather
# than a real filter. See docs/SIGNAL_TRIGGER_LOGIC.md.
ADX_THRESHOLD=20
CHOPPINESS_INDEX_MAX=60

# --- Sustained-trend bypass (structural-reaction filter fallback) --------------
# A steady one-directional grind can run entirely inside the gap between two
# structural levels, never producing a discrete breakout/breakdown/bounce/
# rejection for passesStructuralReactionFilter() to confirm against. When the
# trailing streak of strict trend-agreement bars (spot vs SMA9 + RSI14 >=55/
# <=45 — see IndicatorsService.computeConsecutiveTrendBars()) is at least
# SUSTAINED_TREND_MIN_BARS AND ATR14 >= SUSTAINED_TREND_ATR_BASELINE, the
# level-touch requirement is bypassed on trend conviction alone. See the
# STRUCTURAL_REACTION block in SignalsService.refreshSignal().
SUSTAINED_TREND_MIN_BARS=3
SUSTAINED_TREND_ATR_BASELINE=15

# --- Pivot & Structure Reaction Analysis Engine ------------------------------
# IndicatorsService.computeReactionLevels() maintains a dynamic array of
# structural price levels each refresh tick: the classic daily floor pivots
# (Pivot/R1/R2/S1/S2) PLUS intraday 5m swing-high/low clusters detected from
# *today's* candles only, merged within STRUCTURE_REACTION_TOLERANCE_ATR_MULT
# x ATR(14) of each other. SignalsService uses this array in two places:
#   1. Entry filter (passesStructuralReactionFilter()) — a CALL requires a
#      breakout above / bounce off a level; a PUT requires a breakdown below
#      / rejection from one. STRUCTURE_REACTION_TOLERANCE_ATR_MULT is how
#      close the latest 5m candle's wick must come to a level to count as a
#      bounce/rejection off it.
#   2. Target-snap (resolveTargetPoints()) — targetSpot snaps to the nearest
#      qualifying reaction level in the favorable direction instead of the
#      plain symmetric ATR distance, when that level is at least
#      STRUCTURE_MIN_TARGET_ATR_MULT x ATR away. Per spec this is tunable
#      across 1.5x–2x ATR; defaults to 2x to preserve the existing 2:1
#      reward:risk guarantee — lower it toward 1.5x deliberately (trades some
#      of that guaranteed floor for tighter, more frequently-hit targets).
STRUCTURE_REACTION_TOLERANCE_ATR_MULT=0.15
STRUCTURE_MIN_TARGET_ATR_MULT=2

# --- Dynamic Profit Protection: trailing stop-loss ---------------------------
# Once an ACTIVE position moves favorably, PositionMonitorService ratchets
# stopLossSpot forward in two stages (never loosening it):
#   1. Breakeven shield  — at +TRAIL_BREAKEVEN_ATR_MULT  x ATR(14), stop → entry.
#   2. Dynamic profit lock — at +TRAIL_PROFIT_LOCK_ATR_MULT x ATR(14), stop →
#      entry ± TRAIL_PROFIT_LOCK_FRACTION x ATR(14) of guaranteed profit.
# A stop hit after either stage resolves as TRAIL_STOP_HIT, not STOPLOSS_HIT.
# TRAIL_BREAKEVEN_ATR_MULT lowered from 1.0 to 0.4 (2026-09-17) — see
# docs/SIGNAL_TRIGGER_LOGIC.md for why (trades peaking below 1.0x ATR were
# getting zero protection and fully round-tripping into stop-loss losses).
TRAIL_BREAKEVEN_ATR_MULT=0.4
TRAIL_PROFIT_LOCK_ATR_MULT=1.5
TRAIL_PROFIT_LOCK_FRACTION=0.75
# BREAKEVEN-LOCK-TRAP FIX — a third stage between the two above: once
# favorable movement reaches TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_TRIGGER_ATR_MULT x ATR(14) OR
# TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_TRIGGER_POINTS Nifty points (whichever first), the stop is
# floored at entry ± TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_PROFIT_ATR_MULT x ATR(14) — so a trade
# that ran this far never sits at flat ₹0 breakeven on a pullback.
TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_TRIGGER_ATR_MULT=1.3
TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_TRIGGER_POINTS=20
TRAIL_MIN_LOCK_PROFIT_ATR_MULT=0.5

# --- Stale-position time exit -------------------------------------------------
# A position still ACTIVE past STALE_EXIT_MINUTES without hitting target:
#   - if in profit, gets its target pulled in once by STALE_TARGET_REDUCTION_PCT
#   - is force-exited at market (TIME_EXIT) if the favorable move slips back
#     below STALE_MIN_FAVORABLE_ATR_MULT x ATR(14)
STALE_EXIT_MINUTES=30
STALE_TARGET_REDUCTION_PCT=0.30
STALE_MIN_FAVORABLE_ATR_MULT=0.5

# --- Stale-position SOFT exit (added 2026-09-17) -------------------------------
# A much earlier, stricter companion to the stale-position rule above: that
# one only fires once a position WAS in profit and gave it back. This one
# catches a trade that never showed ANY real follow-through at all — if
# still ACTIVE after STALE_POSITION_MINUTES with peak favorable movement
# still under STALE_POSITION_MIN_FAVORABLE_ATR_MULT x ATR(14), it's
# force-closed (TIME_EXIT) now rather than left to ride the much farther
# original stop-loss. Set deliberately below TRAIL_BREAKEVEN_ATR_MULT
# (0.3 < 0.4) so this only ever fires for trades that never got remotely
# close to arming trailing-stop protection.
STALE_POSITION_MINUTES=8
STALE_POSITION_MIN_FAVORABLE_ATR_MULT=0.3

# EARLY ADVERSE-DRIFT EXIT (added 2026-09-18) — fixes a gap in the rule
# above: that check only fires ONCE, at the STALE_POSITION_MINUTES deadline,
# so a trade that stalls early and then quietly drifts against you for
# several minutes rides the full adverse move before anything reacts,
# turning a near-breakeven "this isn't working" cut into a real loss (seen
# live: a trade lost ₹351 in 8 minutes despite peaking at only +1.5pts
# favorable, because price had already drifted ~11pts unfavorable by the
# time the deadline check fired). This checks CONTINUOUSLY during the same
# proving window (before STALE_POSITION_MINUTES elapses): if current
# unfavorable movement reaches this many x ATR(14) against the trade, exit
# immediately instead of waiting for the deadline.
STALE_POSITION_ADVERSE_ATR_MULT=0.3

# --- Mandatory EOD square-off (no overnight rollover) -------------------------
# This many minutes before the 15:30 IST close, any still-ACTIVE position is
# force-closed at market as TIME_EXIT — derived from the exchange close
# (minutesUntilMarketClose), not a second hardcoded clock, so a 15-minute
# default cutoff always means 15:15 IST without needing to be kept in sync
# by hand if the close time is ever revised.
EOD_SQUAREOFF_MINUTES_BEFORE_CLOSE=15

# --- Dynamic Target Revision / peak giveback exit -----------------------------
# A supplementary protective layer independent of the trailing-stop ratchet
# above: if peak favorable movement ever reached the *scaled* progress
# threshold for this trade's target payoff size, of the distance to the
# ORIGINAL target (initialTargetSpot, immune to any later stale-exit
# reduction), but has since given back more than PEAK_GIVEBACK_ATR_MULT x
# ATR(14) from that peak, the position exits immediately (TRAIL_STOP_HIT,
# reason "Target Revised & Profit Locked at X%") to lock in what's left of a
# faded move rather than wait for the (further-away) stop-loss level.
# The threshold itself is tiered by targetCashINR (derived, not persisted —
# see PositionMonitorService.resolveTargetRevisionThresholdPct()) and is
# hardcoded, not env-configurable:
#   ₹1,000–₹1,500 target payoff → 70% of target distance
#   ₹1,501–₹2,999               → 60%
#   ≥ ₹3,000                    → 50%
# The giveback-monitoring gate itself opens on EITHER that scaled % OR a
# flat PEAK_GIVEBACK_TRIGGER_POINTS Nifty-point move, whichever comes first.
PEAK_GIVEBACK_ATR_MULT=0.5
PEAK_GIVEBACK_TRIGGER_POINTS=30

# --- Target progress milestone notifications -----------------------------------
# Every 10s tick, PositionMonitorService measures how far the live price has
# moved toward the position's ORIGINAL target (initialTargetSpot) as a
# percentage, and fires a Telegram + WebSocket ('signal-target-milestone')
# notification the first time it crosses each of 30/40/50/60/70/80/90% —
# each band notifies exactly once per position (lastNotifiedMilestonePct on
# the row is the persisted high-water mark). 100% is TARGET_HIT itself,
# already covered by the ordinary exit notification. The milestone list and
# guard logic are fixed in code (checkTargetMilestones()), not
# env-configurable.

# --- Telegram notifications (optional) ---------------------------------------
# Get a bot token from @BotFather and a chat id from @userinfobot (or your
# group's chat id). Leave both blank to disable delivery — every trailing-
# stop adjustment and exit is still logged server-side either way.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# NOTE: the refresh cadence itself (every 60 seconds) is fixed in
# src/signals/signals.service.ts via @Cron(CronExpression.EVERY_MINUTE)
# since Nest's @Cron decorator needs a compile-time expression. Likewise,
# the 5m candle interval and ATR(14)/SMA(9)/RSI(14) periods are fixed in
# src/market-data/market-data.service.ts and src/indicators/indicators.service.ts,
# and the CURRENT_WEEK/NEXT_WEEK expiry weekday split is fixed in
# src/expiry/expiry.service.ts.
